fluidsynth links its C++ thread probe with the pthread flags.

With osal=cpp11, CMakeLists.txt checks that a std::thread program links.
libc++ calls pthread_create from its headers, and NetBSD has it in
libpthread, not libc. The probe linked without -pthread and configure
stopped with "Your compiler does not support C++11 threading primitives".
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.

--- a/audio/fluidsynth/Makefile
+++ b/audio/fluidsynth/Makefile
@@ -51,5 +51,8 @@
 .include "../../devel/libgetopt/buildlink3.mk"
 .include "../../math/gcem/buildlink3.mk"
 .include "../../mk/readline.buildlink3.mk"
+# The osal=cpp11 probe links std::thread, which calls pthread_create in
+# libc++ headers; NetBSD has it in libpthread, not libc.
+PTHREAD_AUTO_VARS=	yes
 .include "../../mk/pthread.buildlink3.mk"
 .include "../../mk/bsd.pkg.mk"
